Phase 4 verification report (FR-4 collections browsing)

Commands and outcomes:
- flutter analyze -> No issues found! (ran in 4.0s)
- CI=true flutter test -> 384 passed, 0 failed (baseline 374, +10 new)

What shipped:
- lib/shared/models/collection.dart (new): MediaCollection, CollectionMovie.
- lib/shared/services/api_client.dart: getCollections, getCollectionMovies.
- lib/features/library/collections_screen.dart (new): CollectionsScreen,
  CollectionCard, CollectionDetailScreen, both on the FR-1 shared grid
  delegate, entry focus on the first tile, empty state.
- lib/features/library/movies_screen.dart: Collections header action plus the
  explicit Up-from-grid hop and a responsive header.
- lib/shared/widgets/poster_card.dart: onFocusChange passthrough.
- test/features/library/collections_screen_test.dart (new): 9 tests.

Red state before the phase: the client had zero collection code, so the
collections screen, the models, and the API methods did not exist and the test
file failed to compile.

Two defects found and fixed on the way, both caught by tests:
1. Adding the Collections action gave the header three children. Left to
   geometry, Up from a poster tile stopped resolving to the header and landed
   on the rail, so the pre-existing FR-1 suite caught a real regression: the
   search field had become unreachable from the movies grid. The hop is now
   driven explicitly, and library_dpad_test.dart was updated to
   'Up -> Collections -> Right -> search field' with its reachability
   assertion intact.
2. The three-child header Row overflowed by 4.3 px at the 800 px default test
   width. The title is now Flexible with ellipsis and the field shrinks on
   narrow viewports.

Why: the owner asked for collections of movies to be browsable on the TV. The
server and the web UI already manage collections, so no server change was
needed.

Note on device verification: the live library DB denies the development user
and no server was reachable on the LAN during this track, so whether the live
library actually contains collections is still an open operator step (Phase 5).
